;; examples/selfhost_multifile_a.prn -- real, minimal cross-file fixture
;; for build-files (selfhost/main.prn, 2026-08-28), the multi-file
;; companion to examples/multifile_a.prn/b.prn used for the REFERENCE
;; compiler's own test-multifile check.
;;
;; Real, honest scope note, found the hard way across three earlier
;; drafts of this fixture (a defstruct-based one, then a plain-I32-
;; arithmetic one), each hitting a real, separate, pre-existing
;; selfhost/emit.prn gap:
;;   - top-level defstruct isn't walked at all (emit-program/
;;     region-analyze only ever recognize top-level `defn` forms).
;;   - a defn body that's neither `with-arena` nor `let` at the very
;;     top level falls through emit-form's own cond to emit-tail-
;;     symbol, which ONLY correctly handles a bare symbol tail (its
;;     whole real body is "return <mangled node.text>;") -- a bare
;;     `alloc` call, arithmetic expression, or match/cond as the
;;     ENTIRE body all silently emit wrong/empty C through this path
;;     (confirmed via direct instrumentation, not guessed at).
;;   - emit-let-bindings' own real, narrow let-value dispatch (its own
;;     header comment: "alloc call / plain function call / #error")
;;     further requires a plain-call's every argument to be a bare
;;     symbol (no nested calls, no literals) -- `(+ n 10)` fails this
;;     too (10 is a literal, not a symbol).
;; This fixture uses the ONE shape actually proven end-to-end already
;; (examples/valid_only.prn's own real, working `with-arena` + `let` +
;; `alloc` + bare-symbol-tail shape, domain 4's own DoD acceptance
;; case) so it isolates and proves the real thing it means to check --
;; build-files' own cross-file resolution -- without also depending on
;; selfhost/emit.prn coverage that doesn't exist yet. Those three real
;; gaps are flagged in docs/NORTHSTAR.md's own Self-hosting section,
;; not attempted here.

(defn get-message [(buf-arena : Arena @ :region/buffer)]
  (with-arena [scratch :region/scratch 1024]
    (let [temp-str (alloc scratch String "temp")
          real-buf (alloc buf-arena String "cross_file_message")]
      real-buf)))
